package com.konye.historiq.Core.Localization

/** English-only by design — never translated, per project convention. */
object StringsPrivacyPolicy {
    const val privacy_effective_date: String = "Effective September 11, 2026"
    const val privacy_lede: String = "This page explains, in full, what Historiq collects, why, where it's stored, and what control you have over it."
    const val privacy_section_overview_title: String = "1. Overview"
    const val privacy_overview_body: String = "Historiq is a daily history-trivia app with six quiz modes, a friends list, and per-game stats. What data exists about you depends entirely on how you use the app:"
    const val privacy_card_signed_in_label: String = "Signed in"
    const val privacy_card_signed_in_body: String = "(mock Google/Apple sign-in): your account, gameplay, and friends data are stored in a hosted database so your stats and friend leaderboards work the same across every device you sign into."
    const val privacy_card_guest_label: String = "Continue without login (guest)"
    const val privacy_card_guest_body: String = "nothing about you is sent anywhere. Scores, stats, and preferences stay only in the app's local storage on your device."
    const val privacy_overview_footer: String = "Everything below states plainly which of these two modes each kind of data applies to."
    const val privacy_section_account_title: String = "2. Account information"
    const val privacy_account_intro: String = "If you choose \"Continue with Google\" or \"Continue with Apple,\" the app creates an account with:"
    const val privacy_account_item_name: String = "Display name — shown on your profile and to friends on leaderboards"
    const val privacy_account_item_email: String = "Email — currently a mock value, not a real address read from Google or Apple, since real OAuth isn't connected yet"
    const val privacy_account_item_provider: String = "Sign-in provider — which button you tapped (\"Google\" or \"Apple\"), display-only"
    const val privacy_account_item_code: String = "Friend code — a random 9-digit code other players can use to add you as a friend"
    const val privacy_account_item_id: String = "A unique, anonymous account identifier, so the database can tell your data apart from every other player's without needing to know who you really are"
    const val privacy_account_mock_label: String = "About \"mock\" sign-in"
    const val privacy_account_mock_body: String = "the app doesn't yet have real Google/Apple OAuth credentials configured. Tapping either button creates a real, unique account on the app's backend, but the identity behind it — your name, email — is a placeholder, not anything actually read from your Google or Apple account. No real Google or Apple account data is read, requested, or transmitted."
    const val privacy_section_gameplay_title: String = "3. Gameplay data"
    const val privacy_gameplay_intro: String = "For a signed-in account, the app stores:"
    const val privacy_gameplay_item_progress: String = "Daily quiz progress for each of the six games — so you can close the app mid-quiz and resume later"
    const val privacy_gameplay_item_score: String = "Your score for each game, for each day you've played it"
    const val privacy_gameplay_item_stats: String = "Aggregate stats per game: total games played, average score, and perfect-run count"
    const val privacy_gameplay_footer: String = "This is what powers your Profile screen's stats and lets your accepted friends see your daily scores on the Friends leaderboard."
    const val privacy_section_friends_title: String = "4. Friends"
    const val privacy_friends_body: String = "If you send or accept a friend request, the app stores that connection so your Friends leaderboard can show their scores and theirs can show yours. Only accepted friends can see each other's daily scores — no one else can."
    const val privacy_section_security_title: String = "5. Security audit log"
    const val privacy_security_body: String = "Every sign-in is logged with its IP address, device/user-agent info, an event label, and a timestamp. This log exists solely to detect abuse and is never readable by the app itself or any client — it's written by a server-side function with no read access granted to anyone."
    const val privacy_section_device_title: String = "6. On-device-only settings"
    const val privacy_device_body: String = "Your language choice, whether haptic vibration is on, and whether the daily reminder is on are stored only in the app's local settings on your device. None of these ever leave your device, whether you're signed in or playing as a guest."
    const val privacy_section_guest_title: String = "7. Guest mode"
    const val privacy_guest_body: String = "Choosing \"Continue without login\" means the app never creates an account and never contacts the hosted database with anything identifying you. Your scores, stats, and progress still work — the daily play limit still applies — but all of it lives only in local storage on your device. There's no friend code and no friends list in guest mode, since there's no account for anyone to connect to."
    const val privacy_section_sharing_title: String = "8. Sharing & third parties"
    const val privacy_sharing_body1: String = "None of the data above is sold, rented, or shared with any third party, advertiser, or analytics service. The app has no advertising SDK and no analytics/tracking SDK integrated — the \"Watch Ad\" option on hints is a placeholder that doesn't actually show an ad yet, and collects nothing when used."
    const val privacy_sharing_body2: String = "The app's \"Share Results\" feature is the one exception worth naming explicitly: tapping it hands an image and a line of text to whatever app you pick from your device's own share sheet — that's a one-time action you trigger yourself, not ongoing data collection."
    const val privacy_section_storage_title: String = "9. Where data is stored"
    const val privacy_storage_body: String = "Signed-in accounts, gameplay data, friends, and the security audit log are stored in a hosted Postgres database (via Supabase). Access is restricted by row-level security scoped to your own account and, for scores, your accepted friends — nobody else's client can read your data directly. Guest-mode data never reaches this database at all."
    const val privacy_section_choices_title: String = "10. Your choices & deletion"
    const val privacy_choices_item_name: String = "Change your display name anytime from Settings."
    const val privacy_choices_item_toggles: String = "Turn off haptics or the daily reminder anytime from Settings — these take effect immediately."
    const val privacy_choices_item_delete: String = "Delete your account from Settings → Account → Delete Account. This permanently removes your profile, friends, stats, progress, and score history. This cannot be undone."
    const val privacy_choices_item_guest: String = "Guests have nothing server-side to delete; uninstalling the app removes the local data guest mode stored on your device."
    const val privacy_section_children_title: String = "11. Children's privacy"
    const val privacy_children_body: String = "Historiq is a general-audience trivia app and isn't directed at children under 13. The app doesn't knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the app, contact us using the details below and it will be removed."
    const val privacy_section_changes_title: String = "12. Changes to this policy"
    const val privacy_changes_body: String = "If what the app collects or how it's used changes, this screen will be updated and the effective date above will change accordingly."
    const val privacy_section_contact_title: String = "13. Contact"
    const val privacy_contact_body: String = "Questions about this policy, or requests to access or delete your data, can be sent to:"
    const val privacy_view_online_label: String = "This policy is also available online at:"
}
